 ],
 "text": "On a snowy New York trolley ride, Mary Anderson noticed a problem. Drivers had to open their windows, sometimes stopping to clear the glass. Her 1903 patent put rubber blades on an arm outside the glass. Turn a handle inside, and springs press the rubber as it sweeps. A counterweight kept the swinging arm balanced. Lesson, the hassles everyone accepts are problems waiting for a tool. Download RM to support lively hadtools."
